      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Evaluate $f(x)={x}^{2}-6x+9$ at $x=a+2.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $f(a+2),$ we write down the function $f$ and replace every occurrence of $x$ with $(a+2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}-6x+9 \\\\ f(a+2) & =(a+2)^{2}-6(a+2)+9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(a+2) & =(a+2)^{2}-6(a+2)+9 \\\\  & =(a+2)(a+2)-6a-12+9 \\\\  & ={a}^{2}+2a+2a+4-6a-3 \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-2a+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(a+2)={a}^{2}-2a+1.$",
